<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (This model assumes that natural resources are unlimited and waste can be endlessly absorbed by the planet. However, this is no longer true. A part of this linear model is planned obsolescence - when a product has been designed to have a limited lifespan to encourage consumers to buy it again, which is contradictory to sustainable development principles.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (In a circular economy, materials are kept in use for as long as possible. Instead of being thrown away, products and components are designed to be reused, repaired, or recycled. The goal is not just to reduce waste, but to eliminate the very concept of waste by thinking in closed loops.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
